{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Degree.Lemmas"],"declarations":36,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.c1_isoclinic_of_newton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.c1_isoclinic_of_newton","kind":"theorem","line":310,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ThetaSlopeArithmetic.lean#L310-L314","doc":"**C1's polygon really is isoclinic**: every slope in it equals `c1Slope`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.newtonSlopes_c1_ne_ggm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.newtonSlopes_c1_ne_ggm","kind":"theorem","line":302,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ThetaSlopeArithmetic.lean#L302-L308","doc":"**Door-i, from the polygons rather than from two stipulated numbers.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.ggmSlopes_eq_newton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.ggmSlopes_eq_newton","kind":"theorem","line":297,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ThetaSlopeArithmetic.lean#L297-L300","doc":"**`ggmSlopes` is DERIVED**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.c1Slope_eq_newton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.c1Slope_eq_newton","kind":"theorem","line":293,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ThetaSlopeArithmetic.lean#L293-L295","doc":"**`c1Slope` is DERIVED**: the stipulated `½` is the computed Newton slope. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.newtonSlopes_ggm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.newtonSlopes_ggm","kind":"theorem","line":289,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ThetaSlopeArithmetic.lean#L289-L291","doc":"**GGM is anisoclinic with slopes `{−1, +1}` at `∞`** — computed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.newtonSlopes_c1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.newtonSlopes_c1","kind":"theorem","line":285,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ThetaSlopeArithmetic.lean#L285-L287","doc":"**C1 is pure isoclinic of slope ½ at `∞`** — computed, not stipulated. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.ggmAtInfinity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.ggmAtInfinity","kind":"def","line":282,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ThetaSlopeArithmetic.lean#L282-L283","doc":"GGM's Newton data at `∞`, from `ggm_valuations`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.c1AtInfinity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.c1AtInfinity","kind":"def","line":279,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ThetaSlopeArithmetic.lean#L279-L280","doc":"C1's Newton data at `∞`, from `c1_valuations`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.ggm_valuations","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.ggm_valuations","kind":"theorem","line":268,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ThetaSlopeArithmetic.lean#L268-L275","doc":"The GGM valuation triple at `∞` is `(1, 0, 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.c1_valuations","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.c1_valuations","kind":"theorem","line":251,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ThetaSlopeArithmetic.lean#L251-L266","doc":"The C1 valuation triple at `∞` is `(0, 1, 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.ggmA2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.ggmA2","kind":"def","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ThetaSlopeArithmetic.lean#L241-L241","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.ggmA1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.ggmA1","kind":"def","line":240,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ThetaSlopeArithmetic.lean#L240-L240","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.ggmA0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.ggmA0","kind":"def","line":238,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ThetaSlopeArithmetic.lean#L238-L239","doc":"`L2` (GGM eq-49) at `∞`: `qw·σ̃² + (1−2qw)·σ̃ + qw`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.c1A2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.c1A2","kind":"def","line":236,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ThetaSlopeArithmetic.lean#L236-L236","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.c1A1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.c1A1","kind":"def","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ThetaSlopeArithmetic.lean#L235-L235","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.c1A0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.c1A0","kind":"def","line":232,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ThetaSlopeArithmetic.lean#L232-L234","doc":"`L1` (C1) at `∞`, RSZ frame `w = 1/x`, denominators cleared:\n`−(q−1)w·σ̃² − (q−1)w·σ̃ + (1−w)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.newtonSlopes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.newtonSlopes","kind":"def","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ThetaSlopeArithmetic.lean#L217-L226","doc":"**RSZ §2.2.1 Newton slopes, order 2.** Lower convex hull of\n`{(0,v₀), (1,v₁), (2,v₂)}`. The middle point lies strictly *above* the segment\n`(0,v₀) → (2,v₂)` exactly when `v₀ + v₂ < 2v₁`; then the hull is one edge of\nhorizontal length `2` and the slope `(v₂−v₀)/2` occurs with multiplicity `2`.\nOtherwise the hull breaks at `(1,v₁)` into two edges of length `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.Order2Valuations.v2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.Order2Valuations.v2","kind":"def","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ThetaSlopeArithmetic.lean#L215-L215","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.Order2Valuations.v1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.Order2Valuations.v1","kind":"def","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ThetaSlopeArithmetic.lean#L214-L214","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.Order2Valuations.v0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.Order2Valuations.v0","kind":"def","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ThetaSlopeArithmetic.lean#L213-L213","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.Order2Valuations.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.Order2Valuations.mk","kind":"ctor","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ThetaSlopeArithmetic.lean#L212-L212","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.Order2Valuations","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.Order2Valuations","kind":"structure","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ThetaSlopeArithmetic.lean#L210-L215","doc":"The three `w`-adic valuations `(v(a₀), v(a₁), v(a₂))` of an order-2\nq-difference operator `a₂σ̃² + a₁σ̃ + a₀`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.gs_cumulative_degree_choose","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.gs_cumulative_degree_choose","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ThetaSlopeArithmetic.lean#L165-L171","doc":"The GS cumulative degree in the `C(m,2)` closed form. Records the top-degree\nidentity `∑_{k<m} k = ℓ(w₀) = C(m,2)` explicitly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.gs_cumulative_degree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.gs_cumulative_degree","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ThetaSlopeArithmetic.lean#L154-L163","doc":"**GS-filtration cumulative q-degree = C(m,2).** The Hecke reducer's\nGröbner–Shirshov normal forms are graded by Coxeter/word length; level `k`\ncontributes degree `k`, so the cumulative degree through level `m` is\n`∑_{k<m} k = m(m−1)/2 = C(m,2)` — the top degree `ℓ(w₀)` of the longest\nelement (corpus witness `gb-filtration-jet-order`). Pure ℕ combinatorics\n(`Finset.sum_range_id_mul_two`). This is the categorical grading the theta\nGaussian is (numerically) half of. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.c1_not_bar_fixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.c1_not_bar_fixed","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ThetaSlopeArithmetic.lean#L141-L142","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.ggm_bar_stable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.ggm_bar_stable","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ThetaSlopeArithmetic.lean#L134-L139","doc":"GGM's slope multiset is bar-stable as a set (`bar` swaps its two slopes);\nC1's single slope `½` is not bar-fixed (`bar ½ = −½ ≠ ½`). This is the\nslope-level shadow of \"GGM is bar-symmetric (sinh/cosh), C1 is not\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.bar_involutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.bar_involutive","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ThetaSlopeArithmetic.lean#L128-L132","doc":"The bar involution is an involution on slopes (`bar (bar s) = s`) — the\nalgebraic reason the {+1,−1} pair is bar-stable as a set while the sole\nslope `½` of C1 is not. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.sinhcosh_eq_ggm_swap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.sinhcosh_eq_ggm_swap","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ThetaSlopeArithmetic.lean#L120-L126","doc":"…and `(1, −1)` **is** the GGM multiset (up to order). So the sinh/cosh\n(square + bar-even/odd) operation is dimensionally exactly the bridge that\nevery module transform (Door-i) provably could not be. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.sinhcosh_reaches_ggm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.sinhcosh_reaches_ggm","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ThetaSlopeArithmetic.lean#L112-L118","doc":"**The sinh/cosh twist reaches the GGM slope pair.** The symmetric square of\na slope-`½` solution `f` sits at slope `2·½ = 1` (`f²`) and its\nbar-conjugate `(f̄)²` at slope `2·(−½) = −1`. The pair equals `(1, −1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.pullback_cannot_reach_ggm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.pullback_cannot_reach_ggm","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ThetaSlopeArithmetic.lean#L103-L110","doc":"**Door-i obstruction, slope form: no ramified pullback reaches GGM.** A\npullback of the equal pair `(½,½)` is again an equal pair `(ℓ/2, ℓ/2)`;\nit can never equal the distinct GGM pair `{−1,+1}`, for any `ℓ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.ggm_anisoclinic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.ggm_anisoclinic","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ThetaSlopeArithmetic.lean#L98-L101","doc":"GGM is **anisoclinic**: its two slopes differ. (C1's are equal.) This is\nthe invariant that separates the two modules. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.ggmSlopes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.ggmSlopes","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ThetaSlopeArithmetic.lean#L92-L96","doc":"GGM eq-49 slope multiset `{−1, +1}`.\n\n**DERIVED** as of 2026-08-08 by `ggmSlopes_eq_newton`, from the Newton polygon\nof `L2 = σ² − (2 − qx)σ + 1` at `∞`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.c1Slope","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.c1Slope","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ThetaSlopeArithmetic.lean#L83-L90","doc":"C1 — the proved q-lift kernel — is pure isoclinic of slope `½`.\n\n**DERIVED** as of 2026-08-08: `c1Slope_eq_newton` at the bottom of this file\nproves this value is the computed Newton slope of `L1` at `∞`. It remains a\n`def` so the theorems above keep their shape. What is still a premise is which\nq-Gevrey growth quantity this number is — see the \"order vs level\" note in the\nmodule docstring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.pullback","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.pullback","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ThetaSlopeArithmetic.lean#L79-L81","doc":"Ramified pullback `x ↦ x^{1/ℓ}` scales every slope uniformly by `ℓ`\n(RSZ Thm 2.2.1(iv)). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.prodSlope","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.prodSlope","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ThetaSlopeArithmetic.lean#L76-L77","doc":"Product of two solutions adds their slopes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.bar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ThetaSlopeArithmetic.bar","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ThetaSlopeArithmetic.lean#L72-L74","doc":"Bar involution `q ↦ q⁻¹` on the Newton-polygon slope (theta order): it\nnegates the slope (it inverts the q-Gevrey growth direction). ","signatureChunk":0}]}